<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      PB-TOK-4: one fixed set, deliberately not split across values/ and values-night/.
      Section 5 defers light mode to Phase C, so there is no light variant to resolve to and
      the app must not vary with the system uiMode.

      PB-TOK-1 (S16): these are NO LONGER PLACEHOLDERS. Every value below is the corresponding
      token in internal/design/tokens.json, opaque-prefixed, and android/design-tokens.tsv is
      the checked-in join that says which token each one is. android/gate/s16_tokens_test.go
      enforces it in both directions: a divergent value fails, and a colour resource with no
      row fails too, because that is how "single origin" decays into "origin plus a few extras".

      PB-TOK-5 (S22a): all seventeen colours, not three. The three that were here shipped through
      a join built for the whole palette; the other fourteen (every surface, every hairline,
      every status colour) had no Android representation at all, so no screen could consume
      them and the fence around them was green because there was nothing to disagree with.

      ADR-009 (O2): THE SKIN IS OBSIDIAN. Every value below moved (warm near-black
      ground, linen inks, one champagne accent) and two colours were added (the approval sheet's
      gradient stops), taking the count from seventeen to nineteen. Not one line of this file
      was decided here: the origin is internal/design/tokens.json, which transcribes the
      :root block of docs/research/obsidian-maquette.html, and the gate requires this file to
      follow. The comments to the right are the token names, and they are annotations.

      ADR-020 (W4, 2026-08-27): THE SKIN IS SLATE. All nineteen values below moved again (cool
      near-black ground, cool inks, one slate-blue accent that is still both hero and attention),
      no colour was added and no row of the join changed. Same arrangement as ADR-009: the origin
      is internal/design/tokens.json, which now transcribes the :root block of
      docs/research/slate-maquette.html, and the gate required this file to follow.

      Do not edit a value here. Edit internal/design/tokens.json, which is itself drift-guarded
      against the design source (PB-TOK-2), and the gate will require this file to follow.

      Do not add a colour here either. A <color> with no row in android/design-tokens.tsv fails
      the gate by design. If a screen needs a colour this file does not have, it is either a
      token (add it to the origin) or a DERIVATION of one (internal/design/derive.go, PB-TOK-7),
      never a literal typed at the point of use.

      Each row is annotated with the token it is, so this file can be read without the join open
      beside it. The join is still the authority; these are annotations, not a second copy.
      The tokens' real names carry a leading double hyphen (they are CSS custom properties);
      it is elided in the annotations because XML forbids that sequence inside a comment.
    -->
    <color name="swarm_background">#FF0B0E14</color>        <!-- p-bg -->
    <color name="swarm_surface_card">#FF131824</color>      <!-- p-card -->
    <color name="swarm_surface_elevated">#FF1B2334</color>  <!-- p-elev -->
    <color name="swarm_surface_well">#FF080A10</color>      <!-- p-well -->
    <color name="swarm_hairline">#FF262E3F</color>          <!-- p-hair -->
    <color name="swarm_text_primary">#FFEEF2F8</color>      <!-- p-ink -->
    <color name="swarm_text_secondary">#FF9AA6BA</color>    <!-- p-ink2 -->
    <color name="swarm_text_tertiary">#FF66718A</color>     <!-- p-ink3 -->
    <color name="swarm_hero">#FF8EB4E6</color>              <!-- p-hero -->
    <color name="swarm_hero_ink">#FF0B1524</color>          <!-- p-hero-ink -->
    <color name="swarm_state_attention">#FF8EB4E6</color>   <!-- p-att -->
    <color name="swarm_state_working">#FF6FC3BC</color>     <!-- p-work -->
    <color name="swarm_state_ok">#FF8CC49A</color>          <!-- p-ok -->
    <color name="swarm_state_error">#FFE5736B</color>       <!-- p-err -->
    <!--
      swarm_cta_background / swarm_cta_ink hold the same bytes as swarm_hero / swarm_hero_ink
      TODAY. They are separate resources on purpose: p-cta-bg and p-cta-ink are distinct tokens
      that happen to be value-aliases, and collapsing them here would make breaking the alias a
      refactor of every CTA instead of a one-line edit to the origin.
    -->
    <color name="swarm_cta_background">#FF8EB4E6</color>    <!-- p-cta-bg -->
    <color name="swarm_cta_ink">#FF0B1524</color>           <!-- p-cta-ink -->
    <color name="swarm_tabbar_background">#FF0B0E14</color> <!-- p-tabbg -->
    <!--
      ADR-009 D4.4: the approval sheet is the ONE vertical gradient in the app and the only
      surface besides a promoted slab carrying the strong top edge: the heaviest material
      there is, reserved for the moment of decision. Its two stops are tokens rather than a
      derivation because a gradient's endpoints are chosen, not computed from a base.

      They are two resources for two stops on purpose. A single resource plus an alpha would
      make the gradient's direction and depth a property of whatever drawable consumed it,
      which is precisely the "chosen at the point of use" this file exists to forbid.
    -->
    <color name="swarm_sheet_gradient_top">#FF1B2334</color>    <!-- p-sheet-hi -->
    <color name="swarm_sheet_gradient_bottom">#FF10141D</color> <!-- p-sheet-lo -->
</resources>
